1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =林譚彩霞 (Cǎi Xiá)=
2 CONT
2 CONT 林譚彩霞 (Cǎi Xiá) was my paternal grandmother. She was born on March 16, 1938, and died on August 03, 1993.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother and brother originated from 四九鄉潮陽村 (Chaoyang Village, Sijiu Township).
2 CONT
2 CONT She is the third child of seven children of Kwai Fung Louie Lam (林雷挂鳳).
2 CONT
2 CONT Not much is known about her earlier years, but I heard that she met and married 譚沃榮 (Wò Róng) between the years of 1956 - 1960 while working in the steam electricity plant, in which her job was to put fire wood into the boilers to
2 CONC  power the steam engines (or something like that).
2 CONT
2 CONT IIn 1984, 林彩霞 (Cǎi Xiá) was sponsored by her eldest sister (Ching Hing Lam / Margaret Yee) along with her husband, 譚沃榮 (Wò Róng), and three of their four children to immigrate to New York City, in which they lived in a garage init
2 CONC ially before finding an apartment in her eldest sister's husband's (Roy Yee's) apartment complex in Nolita (41 Kenmare Street Apt #1, New York, NY 10012).
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1984 to July 24, 1993, she worked 12-16 hour days as a seamstress for a Chinese clothing manufacturer factory and would forget to take her low blood pressure medication. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 24, 1993, she experienced an aneurysm due to low blood pressure, and had collapsed at home.
2 CONT
2 CONT From July 24, 1993 to August 3, 1993, she had a surgery to replace the damaged blood vessel in the brain with a blood vessel from her leg, and was comatose and most likely brain dead due to the aneurysm depriving the brain of oxyg
2 CONC en. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She passed away on August 3, 1993 after the doctors turned off the respirators / ventilation machine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 林彩霞 (Cǎi Xiá) is currently buried in The Evergreens Cemetery in Section Nain Plot # 949 1/2.
