1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =雷挂鳳 (Guà Fèng) - Kwai Fung Louie Lam=
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 雷挂鳳 (Guà Fèng) was my great grandmother through my paternal grandmother, 林彩霞 (Cǎi Xiá).
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born on Thursday, March 13, 1913. Her father was from the 雷氏, but it is unknown what her mother's surname/clan name was.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Soo Har Lam (Jenny Cheung's mother), Kwai Fung Louie was from 四九鄉潮陽村 (Chaoyang Village, Sijiu Township), Jiangmen, Taishan County, Guangdong Province, Republic of China, and she had no biological siblings. However, he
2 CONC r mother adopted a son, but it's unclear what happened to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime between 1930 and 1934, 雷挂鳳 (Guà Fèng) married 林洋佷 (Yáng Hěn) and had seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # 林青霞 (Qīng Xiá) - Thursday, December 13, 1934;
2 CONT # 林卓文 (Zhuō Wén) - Saturday, May 09, 1936;
2 CONT # 林彩霞 (Cǎi Xiá) - Wednesday, March 16, 1938;
2 CONT # 林卓羡 (Zhuō Xiàn) - Wednesday, November 15, 1939;
2 CONT # 林卓伦 (Zhuō Lún) - Saturday, April 03, 1948;
2 CONT # 林義霞 (Yì Xiá) - Wednesday, March 15, 1950;
2 CONT # 林素霞 (Sù Xiá) - Friday, July 09, 1954
2 CONT
2 CONT As of Friday, December 24, 2021, I don't know much about my first great-grandmother, but I heard from extended family members that she might have suffered from mental illness towards the end of her life. Probably bipolar disorder 
2 CONC or schizophrenia.
2 CONT
2 CONT 雷挂鳳 (Guà Fèng) is currently buried in The Evergreens Cemetery in Section Gibron Plot #B-6.
