1 OCCU Laundry Proprietor 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Added on Tuesday, May 12, 2020:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT His history is unknown other than what is provided by public records.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Young Ki Chung and was most likely born in 廟邊鄉 (Miào biān xiāng), otherwise known as Miao Bian Township, on Sunday, October 03, 1897.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Year 1923 - Age 26 (Prior to immigrating to the United Kingdom)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He fathered a daughter named 翁玉 (Yù) with Wong Chai Lau in Kwangtung (Guangdong Province).
2 CONT
2 CONT YOUNG TAT CHUNG ''(YOUNG KI)'' was born 3 October 1897 in China, and died 14 February 1952 in Manchester, Lancashire. He married SARAH JANE HAZLEHURST 5 March 1928 in Stoke and Wolstanton Register Office, Stoke on Trent, Staffords
2 CONC hire, daughter of GEORGE HAZLEHURST and SARAH BARLOW. She was born on 25 September 1905 in Burslem, Staffordshire, and died 13 June 1968 in Manchester, Lancashire.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes for YOUNG TAT CHUNG:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Young Tat, or sometimes [That], was born in China and must have arrived in the UK sometime between 1911 and 1924. He does not appear on the 1911 census, but by 1925 he had become the father of Lilian Tat Chung in Stoke-on-Trent, S
2 CONC taffordshire. Two more of his children were born in 1926 and 1927 before Young married their mother, Sarah Jane Hazlehurst, in 1928. The children were all re-registered afterward, as they had originally been registered under their
2 CONC  mother's surname of Hazlehurst. The family then moved to Manchester, where Youn and Sarah Jane had another seven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT When they married in 1928, Young Tat Chung was 31, Sarah Jane was 22, and neither had been previously married. They both worked in their laundry, and their address was 106 Broad Street, Hanley. Young's father was named as Young Ki
2 CONC  Chung, deceased, whose occupation was unknown. Sarah Jane's father, George Hazlehurst, was described as a railway waggoner. Witnesses to the marriage were Ah Young and Lily Lee.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 August 1931, Young [That] appeared on a passenger ship record, sailing from Birkenhead to Hong Kong. He was 33 years old, had been born in China, and lived at 59 Stockport Road, Manchester. He was a laundry proprietor. Also s
2 CONC ailing with him were two of his sons, Kenneth Young, aged 5; and Ronald Young, aged 4. We are not sure why they had been assigned the surname of Young rather than Chung, but this may simply have been an error on the part of the cl
2 CONC erk who may have been unfamiliar with Chinese names. Interestingly, although Young Tat's intended future permanent residence was England, both the boys had 'China' as theirs, so perhaps the intention was to take them to live with 
2 CONC relatives there. We know that Ronald, at least, returned to the UK, as he died in 2007 in Manchester.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1933, Young Tat Chung was listed in ''Kelly's Directory'' (an early phone directory) as living at 50 Stockport Road, Manchester. He ran a Chinese laundry.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of the 1939 Register, just before the outbreak of World War Two, Young and Sarah were living at 59 Stockport Road. Young was a self-employed proprietor of laundry and Sarah Jane was a housewife. Living with them were t
2 CONC hree other young Chinese men who also worked the laundry business: Loy Moy, an ironer; Chin Ha Hey, another ironer; and Leong Sing Leong, also known as Harry, who was another laundry proprietor, possibly forming a partnership with
2 CONC  Young. The names of three other people, listed underneath Sarah's, have been redacted, to protect the identity of anyone who may still be alive. They may have been Young and Sarah's children, Lilian, Doreen, and Charles.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Young Tat Chung's probate record records:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Young Tat Chung, of 131 Beresford Road, Rusholme, Manchester, died 14th February 1952. Effects of over £4451 were left in the care of his widow, Sarah Jane, and son, Kenneth.''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of YOUNG TAT CHUNG and SARAH JANE HAZLEHURST are:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # LILLIAN TAT CHUNG, born 1925, Stoke-on-Trent, Staffordshire.
2 CONT # KENNETH TAT CHUNG, born 1926, Stoke-on-Trent, Staffordshire.
2 CONT # RONALD CHUNG, born 1927, Stoke-on-Trent, Staffordshire.
2 CONT # DOREEN CHUNG, born 1933, Manchester, Lancashire.
2 CONT # CHARLES THOMAS CHUNG, born 20 June 1937, Manchester, Lancashire.
2 CONT # ELSIE CHUNG, born 1940, Manchester, Lancashire.
2 CONT # GORDON CHUNG, born 1942, Manchester, Lancashire.
2 CONT # JOHN B. CHUNG, born 1944, Manchester, Lancashire.
2 CONT # DAVID E. CHUNG, born 1945, Manchester, Lancashire.
2 CONT # CAROLE CHUNG, born 1947, Manchester, Lancashire.
2 CONT # LORRAINE CHUNG, born 1948, Manchester, Lancashire.
