1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The first recorded generation of the 李 family tree.  I was the mayor of the county of 天 台 縣。  I had three sons.  Originally from 浙 江 Shanghai area, I relocated to 新 會 縣 Canton.  I married to  禢 氏.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The poem I leave for my descendants  through which to name the sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT 遣下
2 CONT
2 CONT 各子孫宗派
2 CONT
2 CONT 毓元啓應夫宜奕正履
2 CONT
2 CONT 秩秉睿允昌會成修道
2 CONT
2 CONT 立德象賢希聖學宗孔
2 CONT
2 CONT 孟儒绍周程揚各上國
2 CONT
2 CONT 建績大迁聯芳濟美世祚話榮.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''The Story of Lee Dong (尋根源頭是李棟)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lee Dong is accorded the honor of being the first southward migrating ancestor. He was the eldest son of Lee Hay (李禧) who in turn was Lee Lun's (李聯) eldest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is a little historical background. In 1126 AD (靖康元年) when the Jins (女真金人), a northern nomadic tribe who were the ancestors of the later day Manchus (滿清), invaded China. They lay siege to the capital, Kaifeng (開封) or Binliang 
2 CONC (汴梁) as it was called then. They returned a year later and sacked the city, returned north with their captives which included the two Sung emperors and members of the royal family totaling over 3,000 people. A little over a hundre
2 CONC d years later (1233 AD), this scene was replayed when the Mongolians conquered the Jins.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to clan records, Lee Dong (李棟) was involved with the failed effort to relieve the siege of Kaifeng. From the wordings, he was either a low ranking officer or leader of a local militia which had become common as a defence
2 CONC  against the numerous roaming robbers and bandits (流寇). The heroes of the famous novel Water Margin (水滸傳) supposedly were from this era.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the siege, Lee Dong took his family which included his wife, their three sons, Lee Hon (李侃), Lee Chun (李侚) and Lee Yee (李佁), and his younger brother, Lee Jong (李棕) to Lau-sa Li (流沙里) in Panyu just south of Guangzhou. However
2 CONC , there are writing saying they went to Guangzhou's Gao-de Li (高德里) first. They later moved to what was Guangzhou (岡州) in ancient time but is currently known as Xinxing (新與), in Xinhui county (新會). Lived in Chong-bu Hong (中步巷) whi
2 CONC ch was on the town's western edge, Lai-yee Feng district (禮儀坊). On a modern-day map of Xinhui there is a Guangzhou just west of Xinhui City. Could this be one and the same?
2 CONT
2 CONT After things somewhat settled, by that, I guess they meant after the invaders had left, Lee Dong and his brother returned to Nanxiong (南雄) to tie up loose ends such as disposing of real estate properties. Lee Dong died on the retu
2 CONC rn trip. His brother brought his remains back and he was buried at Shek Goe Shan, Xinhui (新會石狗山).
2 CONT
2 CONT After Lee Dong's death, the family was on the move again. Except for this time they all went their separate ways. Lee Dong's widow went with the third son Lee Yee and the second son Lee Chun's third son Lee Kit (李杰) to Gun-jok Hon
2 CONC g De-hung Li, Taishan (台山德行里筋竹坑). Lee Dong's brother, Lee Jong, and his family went to Shunde (順德) and Huangshan (香山) (later renamed Zhongshan, (中山). The second son, Lee Chun was dispatched to Dai Gong, Kaiping (開平大岡). Lee Hon, th
2 CONC e eldest son, moved to Wunbu, Xinhui (新會雲步).
